From 6833f637150596df1fcf94c64403a4c0fb856f07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:23:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The AI reads the descriptions while the visitor looks, and a
 phone layout that fits

- After a sentence search, the homes show at once and the AI reads their
  descriptions in the background, the homes in view first, six at a time. The ones
  that fit what the buyer asked gather in 'Read by AI' at the top of the list, each
  with its reason in a few words; a home whose description rules it out (a lease,
  another kind of property, a missing must-have) leaves the list. It keeps going
  while the visitor browses and stops when they search again. Descriptions are for
  signed-up visitors only (new /homes/api/remarks, six at most, track=0, never a
  recorded view); others are offered a free sign-up.
- Phone: the search is one short block, the filters one row that scrolls sideways,
  the call bar steps aside on the map (the header keeps its phone button), the 2D
  and 3D buttons and the map hint no longer cover the list, the title is smaller,
  the area-size control sits under the hint, and the list page's count, Map
  button (now navy) and Sort fit the screen.
